  "question": {
    "text": "A point source&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> emitting light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> is placed at a very small height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> above a flat reflecting surface <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> (see figure). The intensity of the reflected light is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the incident intensity. Interference fringes are observed on a screen placed parallel to the reflecting surface at a very large distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> from it.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/fffffff.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 140px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rIf the intensity at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> corresponds to a maximum, then the minimum distance through which the reflecting surface&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> should be shifted so that the intensity at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> again becomes maximum is given by:-",
    "image": null
  },
